<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samarra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samarra is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, founded by the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutasim">al-Mu'tasim</a> as a new capital in the ninth century. It housed the caliph's Turkic slave-soldier army away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> describe the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anarchy-at-samarra">Anarchy at Samarra</a> (861–870), when four caliphs were murdered by their own troops, as the point at which military domination of the caliphate became irreversible.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samarra.jpg" alt="Samarra" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdulmomen Laith Mahmoud (عبدالمؤمن ليث محمود) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%87_%D9%81%D9%8A_%D8%A7%D8%AC%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%A1_%D9%85%D8%B7%D8%B1%D9%8A%D9%87_%D9%84%D9%84%D9%85%D8%A3%D8%B0%D9%86%D9%87_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%84%D9%88%D9%8A%D9%87_%D9%81%D9%8A_%D8%B3%D8%A7%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%A1_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A7%D9%82.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
